commit 0f9781ad8cb631a5d59dca2974f7cf3ea6533e1c
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 20:43:11 2026 +0200

    probe: add IberoBench, TokSuite and 13 language leaderboards; one twin group
    
    auto_probe grows from 21 to 44 benchmarks (702 tasks) with benchmarks the
    pinned harness already ships and this project never evaluated: the IberoBench
    multiple-choice tasks, TokSuite, and the language-specific leaderboards a
    survey of all 244 harness task dirs turned up -- C-Eval, KMMLU, HAE-RAE,
    TurkishMMLU, TurBLiMP, ZhoBLiMP, BLiMP-NL, EVALITA, NorEval, FrenchBench,
    Bangla, ARC-MT, MELA -- plus xquad_es. 85 jobs / 88 node-h at the last
    checkpoint of 600M, 1B and 1.7B.
    
    add_harness_tasks.py writes no YAML: these tasks exist, they only need a
    project entry, and every one is loaded through a real TaskManager so an
    unresolvable name or an uncached dataset fails on the login node. n_options
    and n_items are measured off the documents, never asserted.
    
    What is deliberately absent, with the reason in the source:
    - cmmlu, BasqueGLUE: script datasets, which datasets v3 refuses.
    - BertaQA, and the wnli translations: Basque is in no training mixture, so
      no cell would select it; 71 items over two options need 60 % accuracy
      before the Wilson bound can clear chance, so they cannot inform anything.
    - mmlu-redux-spanish: not wanted.
    - TELEIA: 21 test items.
    
    One home per task set: auto_rf and auto_rfgm are retired and their six and
    two benchmarks are in `auto` (rfgm_belebele among them, its rewrite having
    finished at 52,944 of 53,100 rows). Only `auto` and `auto_probe` remain, and
    --reformulated now exits naming the groups that exist instead of raising
    KeyError on a missing one.
    
    Also: write_tasks_json is atomic (temp + os.replace), because a watcher pass
    reads that file while a generator writes it and a partial read costs a pass;
    and probe_survivors reads its language through assign_language, which folds
    INCLUDE's `jp`/`cn` to ja/zh -- without it Japanese was two rows in that
    table and one everywhere else.

